{"availability":"available","full":"mrslbt/HIIT","name":"HIIT","description":"HIIT Runner. Mobile-first interval training web app with audio cues","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-12T11:41:24Z","updated":"2026-04-01T02:58:37Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hiitfitness.vercel.app","topics":["fitness","hiit","interval-timer","interval-training","pwa","timer","treadmill","vanilla-js","web-audio","web-audio-api"],"demo":"https://hiitfitness.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:49.322Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:49.322Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:49.322Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:44:49.322Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-based interval timer built for treadmill HIIT workouts. Big countdown, speed cues, audio alerts. Designed to be readable mid-sprint.","HIIT Runner guides you through a structured treadmill interval workout: warm up, alternating sprint/recovery cycles, and cool down. It tells you what speed to set on the treadmill and counts down each phase for you, so you can focus on running instead of watching the clock.","Most interval timer apps are generic stopwatch tools. They don't tell you what speed to run at, and they're hard to read from a treadmill display shelf. HIIT Runner shows a large countdown timer and the current target speed in km/h, with color-coded phases and audio cues you can hear over the machine."],"features":["Large countdown timer","Speed display - shows the exact km/h to dial in for each phase","Audio cues - distinct synthesized chime patterns for each phase transition, plus a 3-second countdown warning before every switch","Color-coded phases - amber (warm up), red (sprint), blue (recovery), teal (cool down), green (done) with ambient glow effects","Progress tracking - progress bar, phase indicator strip, and \"next up\" preview pill"],"sourc